particularly towards speaking a language

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:32.030
for the first time and what you think
about it. Make sure that you take a piece

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:38.270
of paper and you jot down these reasons
because if you write things and you take

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:42.680
the time to ponder and analyze, it will
stay with you and you will understand

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.010
much more things that may be
a little bit fleeting, that are going

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:51.420
through your head and you didn't exactly
take the time to properly analyze them

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:56.490
Please do that, that's the very beginning
of your new journey into speaking a

00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:04.050
foreign language. Thinking about,
dissecting, jotting down your fears is

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.760
the first necessary step towards
overcoming them but that's not enough.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.440
I think that getting ready before you
speak is actually important so how do

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:19.230
you get ready? Well, one thing that
you can try to do is to make sure that

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:24.630
you understand the language well. We talk normally about speaking the language,

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:29.510
we focus on getting our point across and
sometimes we're a little bit scared of

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:33.900
you know speaking because we think that
people are going to think we're dumb or

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.980
we can't get our point across, but come
to think of it, understanding a language

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:42.240
is the very first step that you have to
undertake if you want to feel a little

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.540
bit more confident. In fact, a
conversation is always bi-directional

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.700
if you understand things that are being
said to you, you can actually reply and

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.620
nowadays with the technology that we
have, you can actually surround yourself

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:00.180
with the language 24/7 and understand it
and more and more. But the second piece

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.980
of advice to get ready to speak is
actually to speak, and when I say "speak"

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:09.330
I don't mean necessarily speak with
someone I mean you can also talk to

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:14.550
yourself think about the amount of time
that you spend talking to yourself and

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:19.200
with yourself in your own mind so we
tend to think that people you see a guy

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:23.190
walking down the street speaking to
himself you think "oh, they are crazy" but we

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.640
do that all the time there's nothing
wrong with that and you can do it in

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:31.800
your foreign language. Now, when you speak
it though, you need some sort of criteria

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.150
to do that you just can't speak for the
sake of it for the hell of it okay just

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:41.700
you know mumbling sentences without a
direction. Think about what you want to

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:45.210
talk about think about what you like,
think about the person you want to talk

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:49.500
to, imagine having an imaginary friend
you can talk to about something very

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.740
specific, and focus on the essential and
on the useful, start formulating

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.040
sentences that you think you will use in
a conversation in real

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:05.310
life later, because in this way you will
be able to get some processes or some

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:10.500
sentences automatic and that will help
when it comes to having a real

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:17.520
conversation with a real person. I know I
know

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:22.500
I know, it sounds trivial but the best
way to overcome your fears is actually

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:27.780
hit them head-on, face them head-on
think about the list of fears that you

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:33.060
have jotted down and you have analyzed
and think about for a moment if there is

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:38.490
one fear that you had something you were
really scared of and then suddenly you

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:44.700
just faced it, do you remember the relief
that you felt, the power that you felt in

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.600
all of sudden
you felt unstoppable, you know that you

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:53.220
finally faced your fear and you said "oh
that's not that difficult, it is not as

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:57.930
difficult as I thought", and it's not
just relief and again it's a sense of

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:03.030
power that will thrust you forward and
then the following thought will be "why

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:09.450
haven't I done this before?" I want you to
remember clearly the power that you

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:12.780
felt inside yourself when you suddenly
faced something that you thought was

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:16.860
impossible to face. Now you feel
unstoppable but there's one more thing

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:21.900
to take into account: the so called
perfectionism syndrome. How many times

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.970
have you thought before speaking or for
a language "I have to sound perfect, I

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:32.520
have to say perfect sentences I have to
have perfect grammar perfect

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:36.990
pronunciation". That's the so called
perfectionism syndrome. Let me explain

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:41.520
why this perfectionism syndrome gets in
the way of your learning, gets in the way

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:45.840
of your speaking with people, gets in the
way of getting your grammar right, gets

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:49.980
in the way of getting your pronunciation
right. Firs,t we're not perfect, we make

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:52.770
mistakes all the time. We learn through
mistakes.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:55.890
Forget about perfection, that's just an
illusion.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:02.160
Second, every form of growth entails some
sort of discomfort. Third, human beings

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:06.510
literally learn through trial and error
we try, we mess up, we try again, we keep

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:11.220
learning. That's what kids and adults do
it's not the kids are any better they

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:15.330
just don't care. They don't think about it,
they just do it. Mess up, learn. Speaking

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:19.500
a foreign language, interacting with
native speakers is literally the realm

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:24.240
of the unpredictable, we can't control
everything. Actually, we can control

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:30.030
nothing and control is a powerful
illusion they chains us instead of

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:34.080
freeing us. All the greatest who have
walked and keep walking on this planet

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:39.960
know this, they've leveraged this knowledge
to get external results from Kobe Bryant

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:44.310
to Einstein. They did not let mistakes
hold them back

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:48.480
they did not recoil in front of
challenges, they kept coming at them they

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:53.460
kept learning, they had faith and that's
how they succeeded. So there you have it

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:57.540
unfortunately this is the end of the
video but I wanted to make a quick

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:02.750
wrap-up before you finish. First, if you
want to overcome your fears make sure to

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:08.280
analyze them, jot them down, dissect them, 
think about why you have them and that's

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:12.660
a very first step towards overcoming
these fears. Second, it's important that

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:17.220
you do some sort of preparation and the
very first thing that I would do if I

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.790
were you would be to improve your
listening comprehension because

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:25.140
confidence is connected with how much
you can understand before you can speak

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:29.880
Another form of preparation is to start
speaking but you don't need to interact

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:35.010
with native speakers, you can just start
talking to yourself and third, as trivial

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:39.750
as it may sound, you have to face your
fears head-on because that's the fastest

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:45.839
way to understand that your fears were
mostly just in your mind. So as promised

00:08:45.839 --> 00:08:50.010
here is the extra tip I told you that
one of the best ways you can face your

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:54.360
fears is to face them head-on and in
this case to start speaking with a

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:59.670
native speaker but how to do that? So, I
would avoid throwing yourself out there

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:04.560
trying to speak the language in as many
situations as possible because for most

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:09.900
of you it can actually be stressful what
I suggest is that you do things

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:15.900
progressively. So, first and foremost,
choose a nice and quiet environment, it

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:21.000
could be your own place, it could be a
cafe. Second thing is to choose a person

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:24.089
you like. You can find them on the
internet or you can find them somewhere

00:09:24.089 --> 00:09:28.390
at a language exchange or
in your own city but it's important that

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:35.200
it's a nice person you want to talk to
and third, make sure that it's not they

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:40.300
we're going to decide what to talk about
it's YOU, YOU are going to talk about

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:46.660
what YOU want, and that will make all the
difference. A combination of a quiet

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:52.000
environment, a nice person and your
will and your willingness of talking

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:56.170
about something you like will make all
the difference and once you do that you

00:09:56.170 --> 00:10:00.550
will realize that that's your first
small victory within the speaking

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:05.410
foreign language world and then this
will help you to get things to the next

